# clangd configuration.
#
# This codebase is old and multi-platform. clangd's include-cleaner routinely flags
# a header as "unused" in a .cpp when it's actually needed by another build target
# (Win32/Linux), reached through a macro, or relied on for a transitive include that
# the macOS TU happens not to need. Those are false positives here and just create
# noise — see docs/sharp-edges.md. So disable the include-cleaner diagnostics while
# keeping the rest of clangd's analysis (and clang-tidy bug checks) on.
Diagnostics:
  UnusedIncludes: None
  MissingIncludes: None
